==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|u}}
{{wikipedia|lang=fi}}
[[File:Fog in Albuquerque - AAfog3.jpg|thumb|150px|''Utu''.]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*utu}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[haze]], [[mist]] {{gloss|of water vapor}}

====Usage notes====
* The words ''[[sumu]]'', ''[[usva]]'' and '''''utu''''' all describe "visible water vapor lightly suspended near the ground", but at different degrees. ''Sumu'' is the thickest and '''''utu''''' thinnest.
* '''''utu''''' is used for haze caused by water vapor - if the haze is caused by something else, it is called {{m|fi|auer}}.

